Well, this can be a good thing or a bad thing.  I'd feel free to
descend the first 3 Dlvls throwing caution to the wind.  It's helpful
to close all doors behind you so you limit the monsters that can rush
you at one time.  But really, there's no need to stay on lvl 1 for
more time than it takes to find the stairs.

When I started out I avoided playing the "easy" classes and went
straight for what the FAQ said was the hardest: Tourist.  And I think
that's an excellent place for anyone to start because you quickly
learn how to fight intelligently, rather than rushing into battle. 
After using the Tourist 20 or more times then go to your "easy"
classes and remember what you learned.  You'll find they're MUCH
easier.

BTW: the easiest race/class is Drow/Wizard IMO (or really any Drow). 
Give them a try after your Tourist.

